WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:02.980
Imagine your best sales call.

2
00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:07.300
Then come the notes, missing context, and the account executive asking, “Who

3
00:00:07.300 --> 00:00:07.980
did we speak to?”

4
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.060
I built this workflow in production.

5
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:13.020
This repository brings that approach to life on AWS.

6
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:17.260
In Slack, reps can see their permitted skills, then choose call review.

7
00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:22.060
The server verifies the request and their access, queues the transcript, and

8
00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.020
a worker calls AgentCore.

9
00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:28.720
AgentCore Runtime hosts our Python workflow, which loads a versioned skill file

10
00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:29.300
from S3.

11
00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:32.700
That playbook tells the model how to review the call, while Python

12
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.060
controls the tools.

13
00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:38.860
Python asks Nova Lite, the language model in Bedrock, to propose facts

14
00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.520
with supporting quotes from the transcript.

15
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:44.260
MCP gives Python one standard interface to the data tools.

16
00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:48.780
AgentCore Gateway routes each call to code that checks permission and evidence

17
00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.140
before saving in DynamoDB.

18
00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:53.780
The result returns through Python to the worker, which posts it back

19
00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:54.160
to Slack.

20
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:57.480
When the rep asks for meeting prep in Slack, the same engine

21
00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:01.220
loads that skill, reads the saved record through MCP, and returns a

22
00:01:01.220 --> 00:01:01.380
brief.

23
00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:06.520
In my production workflow, Salesforce held the shared record, including buyer intent,

24
00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.460
next steps and call warmth.

25
00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:14.320
That context helps account executives prepare and managers coach from wins and

26
00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:14.660
losses.

27
00:01:14.980 --> 00:01:19.720
With less busywork and fewer handoffs, let your sales organization do what

28
00:01:19.720 --> 00:01:21.880
it does best: win sales for you.
